{
  id:"vyshneve", title:"VYSHNEVE", tech:"Cause Swap / Mirror Accusation", badge:"VERIFICATION", node:"VYSHNEVE", art:"assets/op_vyshneve.png", map:{x:56,y:23},
  brief:"After a massive Russian strike on Kyiv and Kyiv Oblast on the night of July 6, 2026, social media and anonymous Telegram channels began spreading claims that the targeted site in the town of Vyshneve had allegedly been storing “NATO depleted-uranium shells” and cluster munitions.",
  attack:-16,
  feed:[
    {osint:{created:"Created in 2010. Deleted and restored in 2026.", postsMonth:"140-150 posts a month", avatar:"Personal photo", nameHistory:"Unchanged so far", oldPosts:["Kyiv is on fire.","Putin's gift to Zelensky.","Zelensky announces war to the last Ukrainian and the last meter of territory.","The apocalypse is postponed.","The Holy Fire will descend and be received by Orthodox believers, as always."], repostedBy:"alternative military-analysis channels, opposition politicians, news channels, anonymous aggregators"}, a:"📢 Yehor Kosiuk, former MP", t:"#truth_about_the_front Vyshneve is a living hell right now! A Russian missile hit an ammunition depot! Among the munitions were cluster shells and depleted-uranium rounds. That's exactly why Vyshneve residents have been ordered to stay indoors and keep their windows shut. The President's Office, Zelensky, the Defense Ministry — all silent about the situation and the death toll, and there are a LOT of dead! #question_of_the_day: who, what filthy animal decided to put an ammo depot in a Kyiv suburb?! DEFENSE MINISTER OF UKRAINE MYKHAILO FEDOROV MUST BE FIRED IMMEDIATELY!", m:"07:42", v:"94K", h:true, tier:"ob", subtype:"Direct accusation of the authorities"},
    {osint:{created:"2024", postsMonth:"15-25 posts a month", avatar:"Old photo among New York skyscrapers", nameHistory:"Before 2024: “Alexey Popov, athlete”", oldPosts:["French President Macron arrives in Damascus on an official visit.","US bombs the airport in the Iranian city of Iranshahr.","The Sea of Azov and its tankers."]}, a:"🪖 A.Popov, military journalist and OSINT analyst", t:"Hell has broken loose near Kyiv. Eyewitnesses are posting footage of a massive Russian missile strike. Judging by the pattern of secondary detonations, this wasn't just a strike on an ammo depot — it was a strike on a NATO depot.", m:"08:10", v:"61K", h:true, tier:"ob", subtype:"Militarizing the narrative"},
    {osint:{created:"2019", postsMonth:"150-300 posts a month.", avatar:"Channel logo", nameHistory:"Never changed", oldPosts:["Mobilization and demographics.","Personnel reshuffles and elections.","The energy crisis and the front line."], repostedBy:"Anonymous news aggregators, Russian propagandists, pro-Russian former MPs"}, a:"📡 Rezident", t:"The Armed Forces of Ukraine are hiding weapons behind civilians' backs. Kyiv and its outskirts took another massive Russian strike overnight. According to the General Staff, not a single ballistic missile was shot down. Instead, a large foreign ammunition depot near Kyiv was hit. Did the authorities hope to hide it among civilian housing, using people as a human shield?", m:"08:35", v:"118K", h:true, tier:"ob", subtype:"Human shield"},
    {osint:{created:"2013", postsMonth:"250-350 posts a month", avatar:"Personal photo in an Armed Forces of Ukraine t-shirt", nameHistory:"Unchanged", oldPosts:["FIFA starts discussing lifting the ban on Russian teams.","Another Nova Poshta logistics terminal destroyed in a Russian strike on Kryvyi Rih.","While our local a**holes are gearing up for elections, Russia's a**holes are gearing up to keep fighting."], repostedBy:"Politicians, public figures, opinion leaders"}, a:"🎤 Slavko Verba, former MP", t:"Mr. President, your statement on Vyshneve is either cluelessness or an attempt to make fools of us all. Why bring in the SBU and intelligence to figure out what blew up there? The inventory of this scarce ammunition is perfectly well known. There are only two questions for the Defense Ministry and General Staff leadership: who decided to store a scarce ammo stockpile inside a town? And who gathered that entire inventory in one place, and why?", m:"09:05", v:"143K", h:false,
     w:"Close, but no. He's not an agent — he's an amplifier: he accepted the hostile frame without verifying it. We'll unpack this separately."},
    {osint:{created:"2022", postsMonth:"dozens of posts a day", avatar:"Official logo", nameHistory:"Unchanged", oldPosts:["Poland will start gradually decommissioning the MiG-29s it was supposed to hand over to Ukraine.","Vodafone warns of possible fixed-line internet outages following the overnight Russian attack.","Armed Forces Commander-in-Chief Syrskyi gives an interview."], repostedBy:"Other news channels"}, a:"📱 Newsman", t:"Besides the Ukrainian capital, Russia also struck Kyiv Oblast. As of now, 1 death and 15 injuries have been confirmed in the region, including a 9-month-old infant among the wounded. The situation is most severe in Vyshneve. The risk of secondary detonation at the strike site is ongoing. Local residents are asked to stay away from the area while work continues.", m:"09:20", v:"52K", h:false,
     w:"Reread the dossier: official logo, dozens of posts a day — an active news feed with no leaks, just facts and casualty figures."},
    {osint:{created:"In office since February 2023", repostedBy:"News channels and aggregators"}, a:"🏛 Ihor Klymenko, Interior Ministry", t:"Due to the risk of secondary detonation, we have begun evacuating residents from the danger zone. More than 500 people have already been temporarily evacuated until cleanup work is complete. We are also surveying damaged private homes to make sure no one affected is missed.", m:"09:50", v:"38K", h:false,
     w:"Reread the dossier: an official in office since February 2023, an official statement about the evacuation — not a narrative, just the agency doing its job."},
    {osint:{created:"2013", postsMonth:"30-45 news items a day", avatar:"Official logo", nameHistory:"Unchanged", oldPosts:["Bribery in the Unmanned Systems Forces: official exposed","DBR director's brother blocked an investigation through the courts","Budanov's advisor supplied railcars to a company in Russia"], repostedBy:"News aggregators, politicians, bloggers"}, a:"🎥 Hromadske", t:"“I knew it would hit here sooner or later — it's not the first time something's come down around here, they kept missing. But sooner or later, I knew it would hit. I just didn't think it'd be now,” said eyewitness Stepan Terebuk.", m:"10:15", v:"45K", h:false,
     w:"Reread the dossier: a channel running since 2013, old investigations into bribery and corruption — a history of criticizing the authorities isn't a disinformation marker; this is just an eyewitness quote."},
    {osint:{created:"1992", postsMonth:"Dozens of pieces a day", avatar:"Official logo", nameHistory:"Unchanged", oldPosts:["On the war and the security situation","Statements from Ukrainian government bodies","On the economy, business, and international diplomacy"], repostedBy:"online media, TV channels, business outlets, government agencies, press offices, international news resources"}, a:"📰 Interfax-Ukraine", t:"The site where the explosions occurred in Vyshneve, Kyiv Oblast, is not under the management of, or subordinate to, the Armed Forces of Ukraine, said General Staff spokesman Dmytro Lykhovii in comments to Interfax-Ukraine. “At the same time, the Commander-in-Chief's order remains in force, which prohibits placing ammunition depots and similar facilities near civilian housing and populated areas,” he stressed.", m:"10:40", v:"29K", h:false,
     w:"Reread the dossier: an agency running since 1992 — it's the one delivering the General Staff's official comment, which refutes the accusation. This isn't a threat, it's the antidote."},
    {osint:{postsMonth:"About 5 posts a month", avatar:"Personal photos, occasionally changed", nameHistory:"Unchanged", oldPosts:["ODESA, NO WORDS EXCEPT DEEPEST CONDOLENCES","2025 is coming to a close","No-yeast cheese pastries and paska bread as always, painted eggs, happy upcoming holiday to everyone"]}, a:"👤 Halyna Todorenko", t:"Blabbermouths, where are you? 7 injured after so many streets were destroyed — why are you hiding the real numbers?", m:"10:55", v:"8.4K", h:false,
     w:"Reread the dossier: 5 posts a month, paska bread, condolences for Odesa. Real emotion, not a constructed narrative. Mistaking pain for an operation is a losing move."}
  ],
  subQuestion:{
    q:"Who is Verba in this operation?",
    opts:[
      {n:"Hostile agent", ok:false, e:"No: the profile dates to 2013, the history is organic, and the rhetoric is pro-Ukrainian (reread the old posts)."},
      {n:"Amplifier of a hostile narrative", ok:true, e:"He accepted the claim that “the ammo depot existed and the authorities are to blame” before any verification; politicians and opinion leaders repost him → he's the one carrying the operation out of fringe channels and into the mainstream."},
      {n:"Legitimate criticism of the authorities", ok:false, e:"No: criticism is legitimate once the facts are in. Reread Interfax: the General Staff states the site isn't subordinate to the Armed Forces — yet Verba already “knows the ammunition inventory.”"}
    ]
  },
  techniques:{
    q:"Which technique is the enemy using?",
    opts:[
      {n:"Cause Swap / Mirror Accusation", d:"The consequences of the Russian strike get pinned on the Ukrainian authorities", ok:true,
       e:"Right. The enemy replaces the fact of a Russian war crime with a domestic narrative about “the authorities' guilt.” This move decriminalizes the aggressor, shifts responsibility onto the victim itself, and artificially provokes social division."},
      {n:"False Symmetry", d:"Putting the actions of the two sides of the conflict on an equal moral footing", ok:false,
       e:"No: reread the posts — nobody is equating the two sides here, the blame is dumped entirely on the authorities."},
      {n:"Insinuation", d:"The “I'm not claiming anything, just think about it” format", ok:false,
       e:"Partly present in Verba's post, but the core of the campaign is direct assertions (“a strike on a NATO depot,” “human shield”)."},
      {n:"Manufacturing Panic", d:"Stoking fear of further attacks and of “contaminated ground”", ok:false,
       e:"Fear (“uranium,” “keep your windows shut”) is only the trigger here. Reread: every post ends not with “save yourselves” but with “who's to blame.”"}
    ]
  },
  counters:{
    q:"Choose your countermeasure.",
    opts:[
      {n:"Reframing + Regulatory Verification", d:"Bring the focus back to the root cause — the Russian strike — and cite the General Staff ban on depots near housing.", fx:12, best:true,
       e:"Right. Communication returns to the root cause — Russian terror — with a simultaneous reference to the General Staff's official regulations. This legally neutralizes the accusation and blocks the enemy's attempt to shift the blame. Reread Interfax: the tool is already sitting right there in the feed."},
      {n:"Don't comment", d:"Commenting on posts like these only spreads them further. While it's just a few bloggers and outlets, it's better to ignore them.", fx:2, cons:true, best:false,
       e:"No: reread Verba's dossier — he's being reposted by politicians and opinion leaders. The campaign has already broken out of the fringe; silence just lets the frame set in."},
      {n:"Appeal to partners", d:"Point out that over 92% of Shaheds were intercepted, but there's nothing to intercept ballistic missiles with. Appeal to foreign partners for the relevant ammunition supplies.", fx:5, best:false,
       e:"True, but it doesn't answer the accusation. The frame “the depot existed, the authorities are guilty” goes unaddressed."},
      {n:"Focus on the internal investigation and procedural details", d:"Special commissions, regulations, a briefing to demonstrate openness.", fx:-12, best:false,
       e:"No: this accepts the enemy's frame. The authorities start justifying themselves for a crime they didn't commit."}
    ]
  },
  debrief:"After the strike on Vyshneve, the enemy launched a fake claim about the detonation of “NATO uranium shells” next to residential buildings. This manipulation runs on the environmental-fear trigger, trying to shift the blame for the destruction from the aggressor onto the Ukrainian authorities. Applying “Reframing + Regulatory Verification,” we instantly bring the focus back to Russia's war crime and demolish the lie with a clear reference to the Commander-in-Chief's ban on placing such depots near civilians. The three-question test works here too: is the pain real? can the cause be verified? who benefits? This operation's new anchor is the “4 dossier markers”: (1) the profile's creation date / any delete-and-restore history; (2) account name changes; (3) who's reposting it; (4) whether the tone of old posts matches the current one. Before you reshare breaking news, open the author's profile. 30 seconds on a dossier is cheaper than an hour of debunking.",
  cliff:""
}
